      "body": "\n<div class=\"challenge-hero\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">Weekly Challenge</div><h2>Editing</h2><p>Shoot normally for a week, but make the challenge about editing: reduce the entire week to only five photographs.</p></div><div class=\"challenge-duration\"><span>Suggested pace</span><strong>Several short sessions across the week</strong></div></div>\n<h2>Why do this?</h2><p>Selection is a photographic skill. A tighter edit reveals recurring strengths and habits more clearly than a large dump of competent frames.</p>\n<div class=\"challenge-briefing\"><div><strong>Working rule</strong><span>Build a small edited set rather than trying to produce one heroic frame.</span></div><div><strong>Stretch</strong><span>For every rejected near-miss, identify the single reason it lost to the keeper.</span></div></div>\n<h2>How to approach it</h2><ol class=\"steps light\"><li>Read the prompt once, then leave Photopedia and look for a situation that genuinely fits it.</li><li>Make variations. Change position, timing or light before deciding the first workable frame is enough.</li><li>Choose the strongest result only after comparing the alternatives.</li><li>Use <strong>Add my note</strong> to record what changed between the weaker and stronger frames.</li></ol>\n<div class=\"tip\"><strong>Challenge rule:</strong> the prompt is a constraint, not a recipe. Interpret it freely enough that the photograph still feels like yours.</div>",
